# Squall Shelf - the side island of the library's plan The Frozen Horizon (storyline SL12, side)
# A low ice shelf the storms keep pushing back into the lanes: one tent, its guy-lines iced, a stranded traveller's
# things inside and a llama that broke its tether, a polar bear that has found the smell of food. Snow and fog. It comes
# back every nine days until its quest is done. Quest "The Stranded Tent" (6 steps): the tent, the stranded note, the
# polar bear, the tent cache, the llama (the net is in the cache), the weather log.
#
# Built by the recipe player (CIRecipe squall_shelf) through the editor's own operations. Points (metres over the sea):
# the tent's pad at 2 m (r 7 round 0 0), the path up from the south beach at 0 -20; the llama's patch round 10 8.
# (Adapted: the design's "each return a new note" needs a visit counter the editor has not got; the shelf comes back
# with the same tent until its quest is done, as The Returning Islet does without its plate chain.)
include lib_features
include lib_sea
include lib_frozen
# RESIZE 10-24: Radius 28 -> 60 (Height 4 -> 4), the old content moved 0 -17.6 as one frame (push) so its sea side stays at the coast; the island grows behind it.
new
gen Trees=0 Bushes=0.1 Rocks=0.3 Harvest=0.1 BeachThings=0.2 Grass=0.1
gen Seed=13101 Radius=60 Height=4 Roughness=0.3 Peaks=1 Shape=0 Style=1 BeachWidth=0.35 Cliffs=0.2 PeakShape=0.4
gen Water=0.5 SeaRocks=0.2 SeaFinds=0.3 Sunken=0.1 Hostiles=0 Friendly=0 SeaLife=0.3
generate
push at 0 -17.6

# --- Terrain: the tent's pad, the path up from the beach --------------------------------------------------------------
brush flatten at 0 0 r=7 s=20 frames=200 h=2
brush flatten from 0 -20 to 0 -7 r=2 s=20 frames=80 h=1.4
pop
brush flatten at -9.7 25.2 r=5 s=8 frames=40
origin
clear at -9.7 25.2 r=6
push at 0 -17.6
clear at 0 0 r=7
clear from 0 -20 to 0 -7 r=2.5
# RESIZE 10-24 retest: at the new coast the generator's shore ice (TP_IceShore_Small1, about 1 m over the pad) buried the tent
clear at 0 0 r=24 only=TP_IceShore_Small1
clear from 0 -22 to 0 -7 r=5 only=TP_IceShore_Small1

# --- The tent, its cache, the notes; the llama's patch; ice and snow ----------------------------------------------------
place Balboa_DecorationPrefabBase_SimpleTent tent at 0 1 ground sit yaw=180
place Zone_Trigger tentzone at 0 -2 ground y=1
place Loot_Chest tentcache at 1.4 2.2 ground sit yaw=200
place Note_Paper strandednote at -1.2 -1.4 ground y=0.1 drop yaw=30
place Note_Book weatherlog at -2.4 2 ground y=0.1 drop yaw=120
place Placeable_Lantern_Metal - at -2 -1.8 ground drop
place "Box Big" - at 2.6 -1 ground sit yaw=15
place Creature_Llama llama at 10 8 ground
place Creature_PolarBear bear at -16 10 ground
call icerock x=-6 z=6 s=1.6 yaw=30
call icerock x=7 z=-5 s=1.3 yaw=200
call icerock x=-9 z=-8 s=1.1 yaw=95
call icetint al=ice
scatter TP_SnowDrift02 3 at 0 0 r=10 seed=13111 free=3
scatter TP_SnowDrift03 2 at 0 0 r=10 seed=13112 free=3
scatter "Pickup_Landmark_Flower_White" 3 at 8 8 r=4 seed=13113 free=2
call shallows x=0 z=17.6 r=60 deep=4 n=1 seed=13130
scatter VP_CoralBulb04 3 at -42.86 -20.97 r=4 seed=13121 wet free=1
call snowfall x=0 z=0 r=32 al=snow fog=#d0dbe4 fa=0.6
pop

# --- DISCOVERIES 10-24 (optional, no quest needs them): camp + note; TP_SnowVehicle02 + chest; hatch with a chest; viewpoint ---
place campfire_1 - at -9.7 25.2 ground sit
place Balboa_DecorationPrefabBase_SimpleTent - at -6.7 27.2 ground sit yaw=177
place "Box Small" - at -11.7 27.7 ground sit
place Note_Paper dnote at -11.7 27.7 ground y=0.7 drop yaw=20
note dnote Sealer's note | Poor hunting. The seals left when the warm water came up.\nLeft the spare furs and the tea in the box.\nIf you are cold, the fire pit still takes driftwood.
place TP_SnowVehicle02 dvan at 23.1 13.9 ground yaw=297
prop dvan tint.color=#7a8a96
prop dvan tint.amount=0.5
place Loot_ChestSmall dwreckchest at 19.1 16.9 ground sit yaw=237
note dwreckchest Driver's box | The driver's box under the seat: bolts, glass and a scrap of leather.
loot dwreckchest Bolt*2;Glass*2;Leather*2
prop dwreckchest loot.refill=0
call hatchcache x=8.8 z=25.5 r=15 seed=13191 alias=dhatch chest=dhatchchest items=MetalIngot*2;Wool*3;Bolt*2
call vinecache x=25.5 z=-8.8 r=15 seed=13193 chest=dvinechest vines=dvines items=Rope*3;Wool*2;Bolt*3
place Zone_Trigger dview at -23.6 13.1 ground
prop dview zone.id=squall_shelf_view
prop dview zone.radius=7
# REDO 10-24: the traveller buried his tea money where the detector finds it (the detector, from the Floelane, used again)
call treasure x=-30 z=-28 r=12 n=1 seed=13195
prop treasure13195 treasure.loot=TitaniumOre*2;TradeToken*3;MetalOre*2
prop dhatchchest if.open=wears|HeadLight*
prop dhatchchest else.open=message||Pitch dark under the hatch. A headlight would show the chest.
prop dview zone.repeat=never
prop dview zone.message=One tent on the whole shelf, its lines iced - and the wind does not stop for a moment.

# --- FILL 10-24 (RESIZE rework): the bigger island's whole area at Raft-like density - trees, bushes, rocks; free= keeps them
#     off the quest's objects and paths
scatter TP_PineTreeSnowy 22 at 0 0 r=55 seed=13300 free=5
scatter "Pickup_Landmark_Tree_Pine" 10 at 0 0 r=55 seed=13301 free=5
scatter CaravanIsland_SmallRock_1 24 at 0 0 r=55 seed=13302 free=3 ground y=-0.6
scatter "Pickup_Landmark_BerryBush" 6 at 0 0 r=55 seed=13303 free=3

# --- Settings, notes, behaviours, quest ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
info title=Squall Shelf
info author=Custom Islands
info description=A low ice shelf the storms keep pushing back into the lanes: one tent, a stranded traveller's cache, a llama off its tether and a bear that smells food. It comes back every nine days. The side island of The Frozen Horizon.
island on.arrive=message||A tent on a scrap of ice, guy-lines white with frost. Nobody answers.

note strandednote Stranded note | (pinned to the tent flap)\n\nSquall took my raft on the third night. I have the tent, the cache, and Bramble - the llama - when she stays.\nA bear comes round at dusk. I go in and keep still.\nIf the shelf drifts near you: the cache is yours. Take Bramble too. I am walking the ice to Saga Drift.
note weatherlog Weather log | WEATHER LOG - SQUALL SHELF\n\nDay 1: north wind, snow.\nDay 3: squall. Raft gone.\nDay 6: fog. The shelf turns with the current - nine days round, near as I can count.\nDay 9: the same lanes again. Leaving on foot while the ice holds.
note tentcache Tent cache | The traveller's cache: hides, wool, feathers, eggs packed in snow, a jar of goo for the stove - and a net launcher for Bramble.
loot tentcache Leather*2;Wool*2;Feather*4;Egg*2;ExplosiveGoo*1;NetGun*1;NetCanister*3
prop tentcache loot.refill=0
prop tentzone zone.id=tent
prop tentzone zone.radius=4
prop tentzone zone.message=The tent. Frost on the flap, a note pinned to it.
prop bear creature.count=1
prop bear creature.respawn=0
prop bear creature.zone=tent
prop llama creature.count=1

quest title=The Stranded Tent
quest intro=A tent on the ice shelf. Go and look.
step reach|tent|1|Go to the tent
step read|Stranded note|1|Read the note pinned to the tent
step kill|Polar bear|1|Drive off the polar bear that comes round at dusk
step open|Tent cache|1|Open the tent's cache
step catch|Llama|1|Net Bramble, the traveller's llama
step read|Weather log|1|Read the traveller's weather log
quest done=The shelf is empty now - the tent, the cache, Bramble. It will drift on without you.
quest reward=Leather*2;Wool*2;CopperIngot*2

save Squall Shelf
